   "unmapped": [
    "Influence maximization under the independent cascade model on a known directed graph with L nodes and |E| edges; action is a seed set of K nodes (paper's K = canonical m)",
    "Reward is the number of influenced nodes (in [K, L]), a nonlinear monotone function of edge activation probabilities",
    "Edge-level semi-bandit feedback: an edge's Bernoulli realization is observed iff its start node is influenced",
    "Activation probabilities linear in known edge features: w(e) = x_e^T theta*",
    "Learner uses an (alpha,gamma)-approximation offline oracle; regret is scaled by alpha*gamma"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "At round t, the agent receives the reward f(S_t, w_t), that is equal to the number of nodes influenced at that round. The agent also receives edge semi-bandit feedback from the diffusion process. Specifically, for any edge e =(u_1, u_2) \\in E, the agent observes the realization of w_t(e) if and only if the start node u_1 of the directed edge e is influenced in the realization w_t."
  }
 ],
